---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="45–55 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson {page.sequence}</p>
  <h1>Rooms &amp; <em>furniture</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Build a clear picture of a room. First introduce a new thing with <span class="ex">There is a lamp in the room.</span> Then locate that known thing with <span class="ex">It is on the desk.</span> Along the way, separate true <strong>furniture</strong> from appliances, fixtures, and small objects, and use precise place phrases.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">45–55 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">rooms · furniture · fixtures · objects</span>
    <span class="tag">new thing vs. known thing</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min optional listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Follow a fictional studio description.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Choose a form from number and information.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Classify objects and locate them precisely.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Present a fictional accessible guest room.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">Natural U.S. choices include <span class="ex">couch</span> or <span class="ex">sofa</span>, <span class="ex">fridge</span> or <span class="ex">refrigerator</span>, and <span class="ex">TV</span> or <span class="ex">television</span>. The shorter forms are common in conversation. The longer forms remain normal.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved singular and plural existence forms and a surface-contact place phrase.">
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Answer from memory, then check. Say each complete sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Earlier lesson choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="in">in</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="on">on</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The studio list introduces one desk: There <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-hint="One singular desk takes there is." data-fix="There is one desk in the studio." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> one desk in the studio.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The list introduces two chairs: There <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-hint="Two chairs is plural, so use there are." data-fix="There are two chairs by the table." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> two chairs by the table.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The laptop touches the desk surface: It is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="on" data-hint="On shows contact with a surface." data-fix="The laptop is on the desk." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the desk.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Meet the room vocabulary</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>This visual bank mixes several useful categories. A bed and a chair are furniture. A refrigerator is an appliance. A bathtub is usually a fixture. A key is a small object. The categories explain the words; they do not tell anyone what a home must contain.</p>
  <div class="figure-grid">
