    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/couch.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">couch</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/chair.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">chair</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/door.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">door</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/window.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">window</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/television.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">TV</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/mirror.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">mirror</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/plant.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">plant</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/toilet.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">toilet</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/bathtub.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">bathtub</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/shower.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">shower</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/key.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">key</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/light.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">light</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/candle.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">candle</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/picture.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">picture</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/clock.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">clock</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/broom.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">broom</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/soap.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">soap</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/basket.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">basket</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/wastebasket.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">wastebasket</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/radio.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">radio</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/phone.svg" alt="" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span><span class="nm">phone</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A fictional studio for a visiting speaker</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“There is a lamp in the room. It is on the desk. There are two chairs by the table. They are between the window and the door. There is some comfortable furniture in the sitting area. The studio has a small kitchen.”</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which sentence introduces the lamp? Which sentence refers to the same known lamp?</li>
      <li>Which form follows one lamp, two chairs, and the uncountable noun <span class="ex">furniture</span>?</li>
      <li>Which sentence views the kitchen as a feature of the studio rather than introducing it into a scene?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You chose from number, countability, new information, known information, and room features.">
    <h3>Discovery check: choose the viewpoint and form</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">First ask whether the sentence introduces something, locates a known thing, or describes a room feature.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Room description form choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It is">It is</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="They are">They are</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="has">has</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The guide introduces one lamp: There <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-hint="One singular lamp takes there is." data-fix="There is a lamp in the room." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a lamp in the room.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The guide introduces two chairs: There <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-hint="Two chairs is plural, so use there are." data-fix="There are two chairs by the table." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> two chairs by the table.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The guide presents an amount of the uncountable noun furniture: There <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-hint="Furniture is uncountable and takes the singular form is." data-fix="There is some comfortable furniture in the sitting area." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> some comfortable furniture in the sitting area.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The lamp is already known. Now give its exact location: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="It is" data-hint="Use it to refer back to the one known lamp." data-fix="It is on the desk." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> on the desk.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The two chairs are already known. Now locate them: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="They are" data-hint="Use they to refer back to the two known chairs." data-fix="They are between the window and the door." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> between the window and the door.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The sentence describes the kitchen as one feature of the studio: The studio <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="has" data-hint="Has presents the kitchen as a feature belonging to the studio." data-fix="The studio has a small kitchen." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a small kitchen.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: four kinds of room information</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A clear description does more than list nouns. It tells the listener what kind of thing each word names, whether the thing is new or known, and how it relates to the room.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>information job</th><th>useful language</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>name a room or area</b></td><td><b>It is / This is + room</b></td><td><span class="ex">This is the sitting area.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>introduce something new</b></td><td><b>There is / There are</b></td><td><span class="ex">There is a lamp by the bed.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>locate a known thing</b></td><td><b>The lamp is / It is</b></td><td><span class="ex">It is on the table.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>describe a feature</b></td><td><b>The room has</b></td><td><span class="ex">The room has a large window.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">The viewpoints can describe the same scene. <span class="ex">There is a large window in the room</span> introduces the window. <span class="ex">The room has a large window</span> describes a feature of the room. Neither pattern is automatically more correct.</p>

  <h3>Furniture is one category, not every thing in a room</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>category</th><th>A1 meaning</th><th>examples</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>furniture</b></td><td>movable things that support living, working, or storage</td><td><span class="ex">bed · chair · sofa · table · desk</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>appliance</b></td><td>a machine used in a home or room</td><td><span class="ex">refrigerator · stove · TV</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>fixture</b></td><td>something usually installed as part of the room</td><td><span class="ex">bathtub · toilet · built-in light</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>small object</b></td><td>a separate item that can be held or moved easily</td><td><span class="ex">key · phone · candle · soap</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>room feature</b></td><td>part of the room or building</td><td><span class="ex">door · window · wall · closet</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><strong>Furniture is uncountable.</strong> Say <span class="ex">some furniture</span>, <span class="ex">a lot of furniture</span>, or <span class="ex">a piece of furniture</span>. Do not say <span class="ex">a furniture</span> or <span class="ex">furnitures</span>. Individual names are countable: <span class="ex">one chair</span>, <span class="ex">two chairs</span>.</p>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-game data-success-message="Correct. Each item is classified by what it is, not simply by the room where it appears.">
    <h3>Classify four room items</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Tap an item, then tap its exact category.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank">
      <button class="tile" data-tile="sofa">sofa</button><button class="tile" data-tile="refrigerator">refrigerator</button><button class="tile" data-tile="bathtub">bathtub</button><button class="tile" data-tile="key">key</button>
    </div>
    <div class="slot-board">
      <button class="slot" data-slot="sofa" data-hint="A sofa is a movable item used for sitting." data-fix="Movable seating: sofa is furniture." data-placeholder="furniture">furniture</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="refrigerator" data-hint="A refrigerator is a machine that keeps food cold." data-fix="A food-cooling machine: refrigerator is an appliance." data-placeholder="appliance">appliance</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="bathtub" data-hint="A bathtub is normally installed as part of a bathroom." data-fix="An installed room item: bathtub is a fixture." data-placeholder="fixture">fixture</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="key" data-hint="A key is a small separate item that a person can carry." data-fix="A small carryable item: key is a small object." data-placeholder="small object">small object</button>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-tiles>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-tiles>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h3>Useful U.S. room words and boundaries</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>word or pair</th><th>useful boundary</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>living room</b></td><td>a shared sitting area in a home</td><td><span class="ex">The living room has a sofa.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>bedroom</b></td><td>a room used for sleeping</td><td><span class="ex">There is a bed in the bedroom.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>kitchen</b></td><td>an area used to prepare food</td><td><span class="ex">The kitchen has a refrigerator.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>bathroom / restroom</b></td><td>In U.S. English, <em>bathroom</em> can mean a toilet room even with no bathtub. <em>Restroom</em> is common in public places.</td><td><span class="ex">Where is the restroom?</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>closet / wardrobe</b></td><td>A closet is storage space built into a room. A wardrobe is a freestanding piece of furniture.</td><td><span class="ex">The coats are in the closet.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>home office</b></td><td>a work area in a home; it may be a full room or part of another room</td><td><span class="ex">The desk is in the home office.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>hallway / balcony</b></td><td>a passage inside a building / a raised outdoor platform connected to a building</td><td><span class="ex">The elevator is at the end of the hallway.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>These names describe function, not one required design. A studio may combine sleeping, working, cooking, and sitting areas in one room. A home office may be one desk in a shared space.</p>

  <h2>New information and known location</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><span class="ex">There is / There are</span> puts a new person or thing into the listener’s mental scene. After the listener knows it, name it or use a pronoun when its exact location is the message.</p>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Follow the information chain</h3>
    <p><span class="ex"><strong>There is a lamp in the room.</strong> It is on the desk.</span></p>
    <p>The first sentence answers <em>What is in the room?</em> The second answers <em>Where is the lamp?</em> Repeating <span class="ex">There is on the desk</span> does not work because <span class="ex">there is</span> needs a following noun phrase.</p>
    <p><span class="ex"><strong>There are two chairs by the table.</strong> They are between the window and the door.</span></p>
    <p>Plural new information takes <span class="ex">there are</span>. The known plural reference takes <span class="ex">they are</span>.</p>
  </div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>noun after there</th><th>affirmative</th><th>negative reminder</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>one singular countable thing</b></td><td><span class="ex">There is a chair.</span></td><td><span class="ex">There isn’t a chair.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>an uncountable amount</b></td><td><span class="ex">There is some furniture.</span></td><td><span class="ex">There isn’t any furniture.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>two or more countable things</b></td><td><span class="ex">There are two chairs.</span></td><td><span class="ex">There aren’t any chairs.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>In speech, <span class="ex">there is</span> commonly contracts to <span class="ex">there’s</span>. In careful A1 writing, keep plural <span class="ex">there are</span> in its full form. You may hear informal speakers use <span class="ex">there’s</span> before a plural list, but the reliable learning form is <span class="ex">There are two chairs</span>.</p>

  <h2>Choose a precise place relationship</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The reference object creates the map. Ask how the first thing relates to that object.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>place phrase</th><th>exact picture</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>in</b></td><td>inside an area or enclosed space</td><td><span class="ex">The towels are in the closet.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>on</b></td><td>in contact with a surface</td><td><span class="ex">The laptop is on the desk.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>under</b></td><td>lower than and in a direct vertical relationship</td><td><span class="ex">The rug is under the table.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>above</b></td><td>higher than, with no surface contact</td><td><span class="ex">The picture is above the sofa.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>next to / beside</b></td><td>immediately at the side</td><td><span class="ex">The lamp is next to the bed.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>near</b></td><td>close, but not necessarily immediately beside</td><td><span class="ex">The desk is near the window.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>between</b></td><td>in the middle of two named reference points</td><td><span class="ex">The chair is between the desk and the door.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>in front of</b></td><td>on the front side of another thing</td><td><span class="ex">The sofa is in front of the bookshelf.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>behind</b></td><td>on the back side of another thing</td><td><span class="ex">The closet is behind the door.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line"><span class="ex">On the wall</span> means attached to or touching the wall surface. <span class="ex">Above the sofa</span> means higher than the sofa, not touching it. <span class="ex">In front of the building</span> means outside or relative to the building. <span class="ex">In the front of the room</span> means inside the room’s front area.</p>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Sound natural: room words, linking, and plural endings</h3>
    <p>Stress the first part of common room compounds: <span class="ex"><strong>LIV</strong>ing room · <strong>BED</strong>room</span>. In conversational U.S. English, <span class="ex">furniture</span> sounds approximately <span class="ex"><strong>FUR</strong>-nuh-cher</span>, <span class="ex">comfortable</span> often sounds like <span class="ex"><strong>KUMF</strong>-ter-buhl</span>, and <span class="ex">refrigerator</span> sounds like <span class="ex">ri-<strong>FRIJ</strong>-uh-ray-ter</span>.</p>
    <p>Link <span class="ex">there’s a</span> as one light opening, then stress the new object: <span class="ex">there’s-a <strong>LAMP</strong></span>. Keep <span class="ex">there are</span> light before a plural noun: <span class="ex">there-are two <strong>CHAIRS</strong></span>. In <span class="ex">next to</span>, <em>to</em> is often reduced: <span class="ex">next-tuh the <strong>BED</strong></span>. In <span class="ex">in front of</span>, <em>of</em> is light and the reference noun carries the last clear beat.</p>
    <p>Keep plural endings audible: <span class="ex">lamps</span> ends /s/, <span class="ex">chairs</span> ends /z/, and <span class="ex">couches</span> adds a final syllable /ɪz/. These endings help the listener predict <span class="ex">there is</span> or <span class="ex">there are</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <section data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read room category, new-information, known-location, and place-relation listening check">
    <h2>Listen: what information does the speaker give?</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p>Your teacher reads each fictional line once with natural U.S. rhythm and once more slowly. Listen for new versus known information and the exact place relationship. Open the script only after checking.</p>
    <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You distinguished introductions, known locations, and precise vertical and horizontal relationships.">
      <h3>Tutor-read listening check</h3>
      <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Room description listening meanings">
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="introduces one new object">introduces one new object</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="locates one known object">locates one known object</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="introduces two new objects">introduces two new objects</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="locates two known objects">locates two known objects</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="higher with no contact">higher with no contact</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="lower in a direct relation">lower in a direct relation</button>
      </div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Clip 1 <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="introduces one new object" data-hint="There’s a introduces one singular object into the scene." data-fix="There’s a lamp in the room: introduces one new object." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Clip 2 <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="locates one known object" data-hint="The lamp uses the definite article because the listener already knows it." data-fix="The lamp is on the desk: locates one known object." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Clip 3 <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="introduces two new objects" data-hint="There are plus two chairs introduces a plural set." data-fix="There are two chairs by the table: introduces two new objects." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Clip 4 <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="locates two known objects" data-hint="The chairs refers back to an already introduced plural set." data-fix="The chairs are between the window and the door: locates two known objects." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Clip 5 places the picture <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="higher with no contact" data-hint="Above means higher than the sofa without touching it." data-fix="The picture is above the sofa: higher with no contact." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Clip 6 places the rug <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="lower in a direct relation" data-hint="Under gives a direct lower relationship to the table." data-fix="The rug is under the table: lower in a direct relation." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
      <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <details class="thinking-card">
      <summary>Open the teacher script after checking</summary>
      <ol>
        <li><span class="ex">There’s a lamp in the room.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">The lamp is on the desk.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">There are two chairs by the table.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">The chairs are between the window and the door.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">The picture is above the sofa.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">The rug is under the table.</span></li>
      </ol>
      <p>Keep the opening grammar light and stress the newly introduced object or the location phrase that carries the message.</p>
    </details>
  </section>

  <h2>Read a fictional floor plan</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>This plan assigns each item to one area for this exercise only. It does not claim that every home uses the same layout.</p>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Community guest studio plan</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">The kitchen has a stove. The sleeping area has a bed. The lounge area has a sofa. The work area has a desk. The bathroom has a shower.</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-game data-success-message="Correct. You matched each object to the area explicitly named in this fictional plan.">
    <h3>Drill 1: match the plan, not a stereotype</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Tap an item, then tap the exact area named for it in the plan.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank">
      <button class="tile" data-tile="stove">stove</button><button class="tile" data-tile="bed">bed</button><button class="tile" data-tile="sofa">sofa</button><button class="tile" data-tile="desk">desk</button><button class="tile" data-tile="shower">shower</button>
    </div>
    <div class="slot-board">
      <button class="slot" data-slot="stove" data-hint="The plan explicitly puts the stove in the kitchen." data-fix="Kitchen in this plan: stove." data-placeholder="kitchen">kitchen</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="bed" data-hint="The plan explicitly puts the bed in the sleeping area." data-fix="Sleeping area in this plan: bed." data-placeholder="sleeping area">sleeping area</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="sofa" data-hint="The plan explicitly puts the sofa in the lounge area." data-fix="Lounge area in this plan: sofa." data-placeholder="lounge area">lounge area</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="desk" data-hint="The plan explicitly puts the desk in the work area." data-fix="Work area in this plan: desk." data-placeholder="work area">work area</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="shower" data-hint="The plan explicitly puts the shower in the bathroom." data-fix="Bathroom in this plan: shower." data-placeholder="bathroom">bathroom</button>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-tiles>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-tiles>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose the exact place phrase</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You mapped enclosure, contact, vertical position, adjacency, and two-point position precisely.">
    <h3>Drill 2: build the picture from the cue</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Place phrase choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="in">in</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="on">on</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="under">under</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="above">above</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="next to">next to</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="between">between</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The towels are inside the closed closet: They are <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="in" data-hint="In shows that the towels are inside the closet." data-fix="The towels are in the closet." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the closet.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The laptop touches the desk surface: It is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="on" data-hint="On means the laptop touches the desk surface." data-fix="The laptop is on the desk." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the desk.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The rug is directly lower than the table: It is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="under" data-hint="Under gives a direct lower relationship to the table." data-fix="The rug is under the table." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the table.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The picture is higher than the sofa and does not touch it: It is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="above" data-hint="Above means higher than without contact." data-fix="The picture is above the sofa." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the sofa.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The lamp is immediately beside the bed: It is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="next to" data-hint="Next to means immediately at the side." data-fix="The lamp is next to the bed." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the bed.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The chair is in the middle of the desk and the door: It is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="between" data-hint="Between uses two named reference points." data-fix="The chair is between the desk and the door." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the desk and the door.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the information chain</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="there is a lamp in the room" data-hint="Use there is to introduce one lamp, then finish with the broad room location." data-fix="There is a lamp in the room." data-success-message="Correct. There is introduces one new lamp into the room scene.">
    <h3>Drill 3: introduce the object</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">The listener does not know about the lamp yet. Build the introduction.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="lamp">lamp</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="there">There</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="room">room</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">is</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="in">in</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="it is on the desk" data-hint="Refer back to the known lamp with it, then give its exact surface location." data-fix="It is on the desk." data-success-message="Correct. It refers to the known lamp, and on gives its exact location.">
    <h3>Drill 4: locate the known object</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">The lamp is now known. Build the next sentence that gives its exact location.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="desk">desk</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="it">It</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="on">on</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">is</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="are" data-hint="Furniture is uncountable, so it takes the singular existence form is." data-fix="There is some furniture in the sitting area." data-why="Furniture is an uncountable category noun. Use there is with some furniture; count individual chairs or pieces of furniture." data-success-message="Correct. You repaired agreement with the uncountable noun furniture.">
    <h3>Drill 5: countable items or uncountable category?</h3>
    <p>The guide describes an amount of furniture: “There are some furniture in the sitting area.” Tap the verb to replace.</p>
    <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="there">There</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="are">are</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="some">some</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="furniture">furniture in the sitting area.</button></div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="there-is-second" data-hint="The second sentence refers back to the known lamp, so use it as the subject." data-fix="There is a lamp in the room. It is on the desk." data-why="There is introduces the lamp. After that, it refers to the same known lamp and on the desk gives its exact location." data-success-message="Correct. You changed a repeated introduction into a known-object location.">
    <h3>Drill 6: new thing or known thing?</h3>
    <p>The guide first introduces a lamp, then locates the same lamp: “There is a lamp in the room. There is on the desk.” Tap the second opening to replace.</p>
    <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="there-is-first">There is</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="lamp">a lamp in the room.</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="there-is-second">There is</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="desk">on the desk.</button></div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Oral transform: introduce, then locate</h3>
    <p>Say each complete response aloud first. Reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> one sofa · introduce it in the lounge area</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>There is a sofa in the lounge area.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> the same sofa · locate it in front of the bookshelf</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>It is in front of the bookshelf.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> two chairs · introduce them by the table</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>There are two chairs by the table.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> the same chairs · locate them between the door and window</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>They are between the door and the window.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> one room feature · use has</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The room has a large closet.</strong></p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Read a fictional guest-room card</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Room 204</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">Room 204 has one bed and a wide, clear path from the door to the bathroom. There is a small desk near the window. The chair is under the desk. A reading light is on the wall above the bed. The bathroom has a shower, not a bathtub.</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You found the path, the chair’s exact location, and the bathroom fixture in the guest-room card.">
    <h3>Read, then choose the exact information</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="from the door to the bathroom" data-hint="The first sentence states both ends of the wide, clear path." data-fix="The wide, clear path goes from the door to the bathroom.">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. Where does the wide, clear path go?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="from the door to the bathroom">from the door to the bathroom</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="from the bed to the window">from the bed to the window</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="from the desk to the chair">from the desk to the chair</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="under the desk" data-hint="The card directly says where the chair is in relation to the desk." data-fix="The chair is under the desk.">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. Where is the chair?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="under the desk">under the desk</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="above the bed">above the bed</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="behind the bathroom door">behind the bathroom door</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a shower" data-hint="The last sentence contrasts the installed bathroom item with a bathtub." data-fix="The bathroom has a shower, not a bathtub.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. Which fixture is in the bathroom?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a shower">a shower</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a bathtub">a bathtub</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a refrigerator">a refrigerator</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it safely and flexibly</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to disclose your real home, address, bedroom, possessions, finances, family, neighborhood, work setup, location, or photos. Use the fictional room cards, invent a complete layout, or discuss personal details only when you freely choose.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Classify the inventory:</b> The fictional studio contains a sofa, refrigerator, bathtub, key, window, desk, lamp, and two chairs. Group them as furniture, appliance, fixture, small object, or room feature.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Introduce the scene:</b> Use <span class="ex">There is</span> with one singular item, <span class="ex">There is</span> with some uncountable furniture, and <span class="ex">There are</span> with two plural items.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Track known information:</b> After introducing the lamp and chairs, continue with <span class="ex">It is</span> and <span class="ex">They are</span>. Give each a precise location.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Check an accessible route:</b> Describe a fictional clear path from the entrance to the bed, desk, and bathroom. Place a rug, chair, and small table so that the path stays clear. This is a language-planning task, not a medical assessment.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Final production: present a fictional guest studio for 45–60 seconds.</b> Name its areas, classify at least two items, introduce one singular item and one plural set, locate those known items with pronouns, describe one room feature with <span class="ex">has</span>, and use at least four precise place phrases.</div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Say the system back</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “Furniture is a(n) ______ noun. <span class="ex">There is / There are</span> introduces something ______. <span class="ex">It is / They are</span> can locate that thing after it becomes ______. <span class="ex">The room has</span> presents something as a room ______.”</p>
    <p>Then explain the difference between <span class="ex">on the wall</span> and <span class="ex">above the sofa</span>, and between <span class="ex">next to</span> and <span class="ex">near</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You classified room items, chose forms from number and information status, and mapped exact place relationships.">
    <h3>Final quiz: build the room from meaning</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="There is some furniture in the room." data-hint="Furniture is uncountable, so use some and the singular existence form is." data-fix="There is some furniture in the room.">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. The guide presents an unspecified amount of furniture. Which sentence is accurate?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="There is some furniture in the room.">There is some furniture in the room.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="There are some furnitures in the room.">There are some furnitures in the room.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="There is a furniture in the room.">There is a furniture in the room.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="There are two chairs by the table." data-hint="Two chairs is a plural set, so use there are and the plural noun chairs." data-fix="There are two chairs by the table.">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. The guide introduces two new chairs. Which sentence fits?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="There are two chairs by the table.">There are two chairs by the table.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="There is two chairs by the table.">There is two chairs by the table.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="They are two chairs by the table.">They are two chairs by the table.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="It is on the desk." data-hint="The one lamp is already known, so refer back with it and give its location." data-fix="It is on the desk.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. The previous sentence introduced one lamp. Now locate the same lamp. Which sentence fits?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It is on the desk.">It is on the desk.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="There is on the desk.">There is on the desk.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="They are on the desk.">They are on the desk.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The room has a large window." data-hint="Has presents the window as a feature of the room." data-fix="The room has a large window.">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. The writer wants to present the window as a room feature. Which sentence fits that viewpoint?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The room has a large window.">The room has a large window.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The room is a large window.">The room is a large window.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The room have a large window.">The room have a large window.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="above" data-hint="The picture is higher than the sofa and does not touch it." data-fix="The picture is above the sofa.">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. The picture is higher than the sofa and does not touch it. It is ___ the sofa.</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="above">above</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="on">on</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="in">in</button></div>
